  "title": "Climate change science and the IPCC",
  "summary": "The Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change was created in 1988 by the World Meteorological Organization and the United Nations Environment Programme to give governments scientific information for climate policy. Its first session met in Geneva from 9 to 11 November 1988, electing officers and setting up three working groups. Its assessment reports draw on published scientific papers and feed the UN climate negotiations. It shared the 2007 Nobel Peace Prize with Al Gore.",
